<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>Travel the full length of China's Silk Road on this comprehensive 11-day journey from the far-western oasis of Kashgar to the ancient imperial capital of Xi'an. This eastward route follows the path of merchants and monks who once carried silk, spices, and ideas across the world's greatest trade route. From the Sunday Market to the Terracotta Warriors, you'll witness the full arc of Silk Road history — Central Asian bazaars, Buddhist cave art, Great Wall fortresses, and China's first imperial dynasty.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Experience Kashgar's legendary Sunday Market</li><li>Visit the Xinjiang Regional Museum in Urumqi</li><li>Explore the ancient Jiaohe Ruins in Turpan</li><li>Marvel at the Mogao Caves in Dunhuang</li><li>Walk the Jiayuguan Fortress — end of the Great Wall</li><li>Stand before the Terracotta Warriors in Xi'an</li><li>Ride the high-speed train across the Gobi</li><li>Cycle atop Xi'an's ancient City Walls</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Kashgar</h4><p>Welcome to Kashgar! Your guide meets you at the airport. Transfer to hotel. Evening walk through the Old City.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Market &amp; Old City</h4><p>Full day exploring Kashgar. Morning at the Sunday Market, the largest in Central Asia. Visit Id Kah Mosque, Abakh Khoja Tomb, and the maze-like Old City alleys.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar ✈ Urumqi</h4><p>Morning flight to Urumqi. Visit the Xinjiang Regional Museum to see the famous Tarim mummies. Afternoon at Hongshan Park and the Grand Bazaar.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Urumqi 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi → Turpan</h4><p>Drive to Turpan (3 hours). Visit the Jiaohe Ancient Ruins, a city carved from earth, and the ingenious Karez underground irrigation system.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Turpan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan → Dunhuang (High-Speed Train)</h4><p>Morning visit to the Flaming Mountains and Grape Valley. Afternoon high-speed train to Dunhuang across the Gobi Desert.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang — Mogao Caves &amp; Singing Sand Dunes</h4><p>Full day of UNESCO wonders. Morning at the Mogao Caves (8 caves included). Afternoon camel ride at the Singing Sand Dunes and visit to Crescent Moon Spring.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang → Jiayuguan</h4><p>Drive through the Gobi Desert to Jiayuguan. Visit the Jiayuguan Fortress, the western terminus of the Ming Dynasty Great Wall. Afternoon at the Overhanging Great Wall.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Jiayuguan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Jiayuguan → Xi'an (High-Speed Train)</h4><p>Full day high-speed train journey to Xi'an. Arrive in the evening. Free time to explore the Muslim Quarter for dinner.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xi'an 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xi'an — Terracotta Warriors</h4><p>Full day at the Terracotta Warriors Museum, one of the world's greatest archaeological discoveries. Visit all three excavation pits and the bronze chariot exhibition hall.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xi'an 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xi'an — City Walls &amp; History</h4><p>Morning bicycle ride atop the ancient City Walls. Visit the Big Wild Goose Pagoda and Shaanxi History Museum. Evening Tang Dynasty music and dance show with dumpling banquet.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xi'an 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Xi'an</h4><p>Free time until your transfer to Xi'an Xianyang International Airport. Your Silk Road journey from west to east concludes.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

